<body>
<h1>HSC VET Construction: Full Paper Game Plan</h1>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> This guide aligns the 2021-2025 paper patterns with the Canva Section III game plan.</p>

<h2>1. HSC Marking Context</h2>
<p>The Canva guide separates school-based assessment from NESA marks. For exam preparation, students need to know that the HSC exam is a major part of the final picture, so timed exam technique matters.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>School-based assessment</th><th>NESA marks</th></tr>
<tr><td>Industry Study Assessment Task, Production Video support task and Trial HSC Exam.</td><td>Major Project, Portfolio and HSC Exam components.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>2. Recommended Exam Time Split</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Section</th><th>Recommended time</th><th>Game plan</th></tr>
<tr><td>Section I</td><td>10 minutes</td><td>Move steadily through multiple choice. Watch for best, first, most appropriate and image-based clues.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Section II</td><td>20 minutes</td><td>Answer short responses clearly. Use correct construction terms, units and examples.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Section III</td><td>60 minutes</td><td>Deconstruct, plan and communicate the extended response. Do not sacrifice planning time.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>3. The Paper Structure Is Stable</h2>
<p>The full HSC paper keeps returning to a familiar structure. Students should prepare for the whole paper rather than only memorising past questions.</p>

<h2>4. Section I: Multiple Choice Patterns</h2>
<ul>
<li>Images matter: tools, signs, plans, shapes and site diagrams appear often.</li>
<li>The wording often asks for the most appropriate, best, first or primary option.</li>
<li>Many questions are small applied scenarios, not just definitions.</li>
<li>Maths questions are short but need careful units and dimensions.</li>
<li>Safety and environmental questions often hide inside ordinary site situations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Section II: Short Answer Patterns</h2>
<p>Short answer questions test whether students can explain construction knowledge clearly and apply it to a workplace example.</p>

<h2>6. Section III: Extended Response Game Plan</h2>
<p>The long response often looks low-order because it may use familiar verbs such as describe or explain. The full marks are in the depth words.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Deconstruct:</strong> find the verb, depth words, scenario and who is involved.</li>
<li><strong>Plan:</strong> build 4-5 points using topic, explain, example, positives, negatives and link / judgement.</li>
<li><strong>Communicate:</strong> write clear paragraphs with construction examples and a link back to the question.</li>
</ol>

<h2>7. High-Value Revision Priorities</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tools:</strong> identify, use, maintain, check and select safely.</li>
<li><strong>Plans:</strong> read site plans, floor plans, elevations, cross-sections, symbols, specifications and scale.</li>
<li><strong>Maths:</strong> practise perimeter, area, volume, ratios, cost, wastage, labour and delivery.</li>
<li><strong>WHS:</strong> apply the hierarchy of control, PPE, SWMS, manual handling and safe work procedures.</li>
<li><strong>Environment:</strong> explain erosion control, waste reduction, reusable materials, sustainability and resource efficiency.</li>
<li><strong>Workplace:</strong> explain teamwork, communication, conflict, sequencing and trade coordination.</li>
<li><strong>Materials:</strong> revise concrete, timber, bricks, sand, aggregate, excavation, slabs, paving and fencing.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Whole-Paper Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>Can I identify common tools from images and describe their use?</li>
<li>Can I read basic plans and explain what information they provide?</li>
<li>Can I complete job-site maths with correct units?</li>
<li>Can I apply WHS controls to a real hazard?</li>
<li>Can I explain environmental strategies with practical examples?</li>
<li>Can I link communication and teamwork to site outcomes?</li>
<li>Can I turn a describe or explain question into a deeper answer using the depth words?</li>
</ul>

<h2>Bottom Line</h2>
<p>The Construction papers are predictable in the skills they test. Prepare for the pattern, manage the time, and give Section III enough planning space.</p>
<p><strong>Sources:</strong> HSC VET Construction examination papers, 2021-2025, and the Section III Canva lesson structure.</p>
